From  Corollary 3 in \cite{boissonnat2017reach} bounds the maximal angle between the tangent spaces at two points on $\mathcal{M}$ through their Euclidean distance and $\tau$.
	Namely, let $p_1, p_2 \in \mathcal{M}$
	\[
	sin(\angle_{\max}(T_{p_1}\mathcal{M}, T_{p_2}\mathcal{M})/2) \leq\frac{\norm{p_1 - p_2}}{2\tau}
	.\]
	Therefore, in our case we obtain,
	\begin{equation} \sin(\angle_{\max} (T_{x+y}\mathcal{M}, T_{p}\mathcal{M})/2) \leq \frac{\sqrt{\norm{x_H}^2 + \|y\|^2}}{2\tau}
	.\end{equation}

